> If you don't see a "Fix Geometries" tool directly in your version of QGIS, you can use an alternative method to repair invalid geometries. Here's how:
> 
> ### Method 1: Using the Geometry Checker Plugin
> 1. **Install the Plugin** (if not already installed):
>    - Go to `Plugins` > `Manage and Install Plugins`.
>    - Search for **Geometry Checker**.
>    - Install it if it isn’t already enabled.
> 
> 2. **Run Geometry Checker**:
>    - After installation, go to `Vector` > `Geometry Tools` > `Geometry Checker`.
>    - In the Geometry Checker dialog, select your layer and choose the checks you want to perform (e.g., "Check valid geometry").
>    - Click **Run**.
> 
> 3. **Fix Invalid Geometries**:
>    - In the results window, you can see which geometries are invalid. 
>    - To fix them, you will need to select invalid features and either delete or edit them manually, or use the **"Repair"** function within the Geometry Checker.
> 
> ### Method 2: Using the "Vector Geometry" Options
> 1. **Select Invalid Features**:
>    - After identifying invalid features from the Geometry Checker, you may want to select them on the map.
> 
> 2. **Export using Special Options**:
>    - Go to `Processing` > `Toolbox`.
>    - Search for **"Vector Geometry"** and choose **"Fix Geometries"** from the list.
>    - Select your layer and run the tool to create a new layer with fixed geometries.
> 
> ### Method 3: Manual Editing
> 1. **Edit Incorrect Features**:
>    - You can manually edit problematic features using the **Node Tool** in the **Digitizing Toolbar**. Select the feature, and then modify the vertices until the shape is valid.
> 
> 2. **Use `Simplify` or `Smooth` Tools**:
>    - Sometimes, simplifying or smoothing the geometry can fix issues without manual editing:
>      - Go to `Vector` > `Geometry Tools` > `Simplify Geometries` or `Smooth Geometries`.
> 
> ### Final Steps
> - Once you have repaired any invalid geometries, proceed to merge the polygons as described earlier. 
> - Be sure to export your final layer to a Shapefile format after ensuring all geometries are valid.
> 
> If you run into any issues or have further questions, feel free to ask!
